-- title:
--   Serre vanishing for twists along a finite projective presentation
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be a field, $X$ a scheme and $f : X \to \operatorname{Spec} k$ a separated morphism. Let $\mathcal L$ be an $\mathcal O_X$-module object of `X.Modules` that is invertible in the sense of `Scheme.Modules.IsInvertible`, i.e. every point of $X$ has an open neighbourhood $U$ on which the pullback of $\mathcal L$ along $U \hookrightarrow X$ is isomorphic to the unit sheaf of modules. Let $N$ be a natural number and let $\mathfrak P$ be a `ProjPresentation` of $\mathcal L$ over $f$ of size $N$: sections $\sigma_i \in \Gamma(\mathcal L, \top)$ for $i \in \mathrm{Fin}(N+1)$, a morphism $\varphi = \mathfrak P.\mathrm{toProj} : X \to \operatorname{Proj}$ of the homogeneous subalgebra of $k[X_0,\dots,X_N]$ with $\varphi$ followed by the structure morphism $\mathbb P^N_k \to \operatorname{Spec} k$ equal to $f$, the requirement that on every open $V$ contained in $\varphi^{-1}D(X_i)$ the map $g \mapsto g \cdot \sigma_i|_V$ is a bijection $\Gamma(X,V) \to \Gamma(\mathcal L,V)$, and the relations $\varphi^\#(X_j/X_i) \cdot \sigma_i = \sigma_j$ on $\varphi^{-1}D(X_i)$. Assume $\varphi$ is finite, and let $\mathcal F$ be a further invertible object of `X.Modules`. The conclusion asserts the existence of $m_0 \in \mathbb N$ such that for every $m \ge m_0$, every ordered affine cover $\mathfrak W$ of $X$ (a finite linearly ordered index type together with affine opens whose supremum is $\top$) and every $i \in \mathbb N$, the module $\mathrm{HSucc}\ \mathfrak W\ i$ of the module-presheaf `OModulePresheaf.ofModules f (𝓕 ⊗ 𝓛.tensorPow m)` — the quotient of $\ker d^{i+1}$ by the image of $d^{i}$ in the ordered Čech complex, so the degree-$(i+1)$ Čech cohomology of $\mathcal F \otimes \mathcal L^{\otimes m}$ on $\mathfrak W$ — is a subsingleton, i.e. vanishes. Here $\mathcal L^{\otimes m}$ is defined by $\mathcal L^{\otimes 0} = \mathbf 1$ and $\mathcal L^{\otimes (n+1)} = \mathcal L^{\otimes n} \otimes \mathcal L$.
--
--   This is Serre's vanishing theorem in the form used in the project: all higher Čech cohomology of $\mathcal F \otimes \mathcal L^{\otimes m}$ vanishes for $m$ large, uniformly in the degree and in the chosen finite ordered affine cover, under the hypothesis that $\mathcal L$ is generated by $N+1$ sections defining a finite morphism to $\mathbb P^N_k$. It feeds the cohomological vanishing statements for polarised abelian varieties and the construction of finite projective towers for fake elliptic curves in the Čerednik–Drinfeld part of the development.
